--TEST--
A connection from `open` with no `base` has nowhere to start a search, so a search that names no `base` throws `LogicError` and one that names a `base` runs
--SKIPIF--
<?nvs
// The case needs the `samba-ad` server from `tests/db/compose.yaml`. Where it
// does not answer, the case is skipped, unless `NVS_LDAP_SAMBA` is set: CI's
// Linux leg runs the server and sets it, so a missing server fails there.
try {
    Core\Ldap::open({
        url: "ldap://127.0.0.1:16389",
        user: "CN=Administrator,CN=Users,DC=example,DC=test",
        password: "Novis-test-1",
        tls: Core\Ldap::Tls::None,
    });
} catch (Core\Ldap\LdapError $down) {
    if ($down->kind != Core\Ldap\LdapError::Kind::Unavailable || Core\Env::get("NVS_LDAP_SAMBA") != null) {
        throw $down;
    }
    echo "skip - ", $down->message, "\n";
}
--FILE--
<?nvs
// This connection sends its password without TLS. Only the test server on
// this machine may be reached that way, and the case is skipped where it is
// not running.
var $corp = Core\Ldap::open({
    url: "ldap://127.0.0.1:16389",
    user: "CN=Administrator,CN=Users,DC=example,DC=test",
    password: "Novis-test-1",
    tls: Core\Ldap::Tls::None,
});
try {
    var $none = $corp->search(Core\Ldap\Filter::present("objectClass"));
    echo "no error", "\n";
} catch (LogicError $e) {
    echo "LogicError: ", $e->message, "\n";
}
int $found = 0;
var $users = $corp->search(Core\Ldap\Filter::present("objectClass"), {
    base: "CN=Users,DC=example,DC=test",
    scope: Core\Ldap\Connection::Scope::Base,
});
foreach ($users as Core\Ldap\Entry $entry) {
    $found = $found + 1;
}
echo "with a base: ", $found, "\n";
--COPY--
../../db/ca.crt
--FILE nvs.toml--
[capabilities.ldap]
open = ["127.0.0.1"]
cleartext = ["127.0.0.1"]

[capabilities.net]
internal = ["127.0.0.1"]
--EXPECT--
LogicError: Core\Ldap\Connection::search: the search has no `base`. Give one, such as `{ base: 'DC=example,DC=test' }`, or set `base` in the `[ldap]` block
with a base: 1
